# Local settings for the ingestion worker. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored — it holds a token, and this repo holds personal study
# notes. Read at worker startup from, in order: $ROOTED_ENV, this repo, and
# beside `rooted.db` in the app data directory. Anything already exported in
# your shell wins; the file never overrides it.
#
# Take effect when the worker restarts, which means when the app restarts.

# --- Speaker labels (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# Who said what in a recording. Needs all three:
#   1. sidecar/.venv/bin/pip install "pyannote.audio>=3.1"
#   2. accept the conditions on hf.co for EACH of:
#        pyannote/speaker-diarization-3.1   (the pipeline)
#        pyannote/segmentation-3.0          (loaded underneath)
#        pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1
#      The last one isn't in 3.1's config: pyannote 4 clusters with PLDA
#      weights that live there, whichever checkpoint you name.
#   3. a read token from hf.co/settings/tokens, here:
# HUGGINGFACE_TOKEN=hf_...
#
# Without it transcripts simply don't say who was talking, which is better
# than guessing at speaker changes. Nothing else depends on it.

# --- Cloud second opinion on a scan (optional) ------------------------------
# Lets you re-read a scanned page's lines with Claude when on-device OCR can't
# manage the handwriting. Off unless both of these are true:
#   1. sidecar/.venv/bin/pip install anthropic
#   2. a key here:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
# This is the only way anything in Rooted leaves your machine, and it never
# happens by itself: you ask for it per page, the app says what is sent
# (cropped lines from that page — not the note, its metadata, or any other
# document), and what comes back still goes through review.
#
# The model, if you want a different one. Default: claude-opus-5.
# ROOTED_CLOUD_OCR_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# --- Transcription (optional) ----------------------------------------------
# Whisper model for recordings: tiny | base | small | medium | large-v3.
# Bigger is more accurate and slower, and is downloaded on first use.
# Default: base.
# ROOTED_WHISPER_MODEL=small

# --- Not settable here ------------------------------------------------------
# ROOTED_DB, ROOTED_WORKER and ROOTED_PYTHON are ignored if you put them in
# this file, on purpose: the app and the worker have to agree about them, and
# the app doesn't read this file. Export them in the shell that starts the app.
